cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Ghost Lows, please cite the software (this file). Benchmark results should
  also name the benchmark version they were computed on. Cite the datasets and
  simulator you use as listed in docs/DATA.md and docs/CITATIONS.md.
title: "Ghost Lows: an open benchmark for real-time CGM low-glucose alarms under sensor faults"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Pranav
    family-names: Karakala Reddy
version: 0.0.1
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pkarakala/ghost-lows"
abstract: >-
  An open benchmark that scores real-time continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) low-glucose
  alarms on lows caught, false alarms per day and minutes of warning under a mixed
  sensor-fault suite (pressure-induced sensor attenuation, dropout, stale readings, drift,
  spikes), with a controlled ablation of what insulin and carbohydrate context adds.
  Research software; not a medical device.
keywords:
  - continuous glucose monitoring
  - hypoglycaemia alarms
  - compression artifacts
  - pressure-induced sensor attenuation
  - benchmark
  - type 1 diabetes
references:
  - type: software
    title: simglucose
    authors:
      - given-names: Jinyu
        family-names: Xie
    version: 0.2.11
    repository-code: "https://github.com/jxx123/simglucose"
  - type: article
    title: Modeling Transient Disconnections and Compression Artifacts of Continuous Glucose Sensors
    authors:
      - family-names: Facchinetti
        given-names: Andrea
      - family-names: Del Favero
        given-names: Simone
      - family-names: Sparacino
        given-names: Giovanni
      - family-names: Cobelli
        given-names: Claudio
    journal: Diabetes Technology & Therapeutics
    year: 2016
    volume: 18
    issue: 4
    start: 264
    end: 272
    doi: 10.1089/dia.2015.0250
